4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,588
A piano lands on our shipment. Cups, bread—the whole delivery is ruined. Unlikely? Sure.

5
00:00:23,588 --> 00:00:30,647
But a damaged shipment, right before you need it? That happens. And the customers are

6
00:00:30,647 --> 00:00:33,000
still going to show up.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:41,654
I know where to get enough to keep us going. So I tell my buyer: ‘The shipment’s ruined.

8
00:00:41,654 --> 00:00:48,385
I’m picking up emergency supplies for the next few days. Please arrange replacement cups

9
00:00:48,385 --> 00:00:56,077
and bread as quickly as possible. The cups can come from the online store. Our bakery

10
00:00:56,077 --> 00:00:58,000
