11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,974
The buyer takes it from there. For the cups, it checks the right product, the quantity,

12
00:01:04,974 --> 00:01:11,513
and the quickest delivery available from the online store. It gets the purchase ready for

13
00:01:11,513 --> 00:01:15,000
approval while I’m out handling the immediate problem.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:23,627
The bread takes a different route. Our bakery works by email, so the buyer writes to them

15
00:01:23,627 --> 00:01:32,761
with what we need and asks how soon they can deliver. They reply with a price, but haven’t

16
00:01:32,761 --> 00:01:40,373
confirmed the delivery time. The buyer follows up, gets that detail, and puts the answer

17
00:01:40,373 --> 00:01:48,493
together. I haven’t had to call the bakery, chase the reply, or copy anything into a

18
00:01:48,493 --> 00:01:49,000
