19
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:56,435
What comes back to me is a plan for both: the cups, the bread, what each will cost, and

20
00:01:56,435 --> 00:02:03,478
when each can arrive. If one leaves us short, I need to know. Otherwise, I can review the

21
00:02:03,478 --> 00:02:07,000
terms and let the buyer get on with it.

22
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:14,907
Once I approve, the buyer places the cup order online and sends the bread order to the

23
00:02:14,907 --> 00:02:21,419
bakery. It checks the store’s order confirmation and the bakery’s email reply against what

24
00:02:21,419 --> 00:02:27,000
